      "url": "https://www.last.fm/music/Scritti+Politti/Cupid+&+Psyche+85",
      "wiki_content": "Cupid & Psyche 85 is the second studio album by the British pop band Scritti Politti, released in June 1985 by Virgin Records in the UK and Warner Bros. Records in the US. The album marks a radical departure from the raw, post-punk and reggae-influenced sounds of their debut, Songs to Remember, signaling a shift toward a highly polished, technologically advanced synth-pop and sophisti-pop aesthetic.\n\nLed by singer-songwriter Green Gartside, the album was crafted alongside keyboardist David Gamson and drummer Fred Maher. The production is renowned for its meticulous attention to detail and extensive use of state-of-the-art digital technology of the era, including the Fairlight CMI and the Synclavier. This \"glossy\" sound was further refined by legendary producer Arif Mardin, who produced three of the album's tracks. The result was a record that deconstructed pop music while simultaneously embracing its commercial appeal.\n\nUpon release, the album was a critical and commercial triumph. It spawned several hit singles, including \"Wood Beez (Pray Like Aretha Franklin),\" \"Absolute,\" \"The Word Girl,\" and \"Perfect Way.\" The latter became the band's biggest hit in the United States, reaching number 11 on the Billboard Hot 100. The album's sophisticated harmonic structures caught the ear of jazz legend Miles Davis, who notably covered \"Perfect Way\" on his 1986 album, Tutu.\n\nDecades later, Cupid & Psyche 85 remains cited as a landmark release of the 1980s, influencing a wide range of artists from the worlds of pop, R&B, and electronic music. It was followed three years later by Provision, which continued the polished production style established on this record. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Scritti+Politti/Cupid+&+Psyche+85\">Read more on Last.fm</a>. User-contributed text is available under the Creative Commons By-SA License; additional terms may apply.",
      "wiki_summary": "Cupid & Psyche 85 is the second studio album by the British pop band Scritti Politti, released in June 1985 by Virgin Records in the UK and Warner Bros. Records in the US. The album marks a radical departure from the raw, post-punk and reggae-influenced sounds of their debut, Songs to Remember, signaling a shift toward a highly polished, technologically advanced synth-pop and sophisti-pop aesthetic. Led by singer-songwriter Green Gartside, the album was crafted alongside keyboardist David Gamson and drummer Fred Maher. The production is renowned for its meticulous attention to detail and extensive use of state-of-the-art digital technology of <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Scritti+Politti/Cupid+&+Psyche+85\">Read more on Last.fm</a>."
    },
    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Cupid & Psyche 85 is the second studio album by the British pop band Scritti Politti, originally released on June 10, 1985, by Virgin Records, and it remains the group's most commercially successful work, peaking at number five on the UK Albums Chart and earning a gold certification for 100,000 copies sold . Frontman Green Gartside fully embraced commercial pop stylings and state-of-the-art studio production on this record, weaving shimmering synths with the heat of classic funk to create a sound described as a fusion of synth-pop, art-pop, electro-funk, and sophisti-pop . The album's lyrics reflect Gartside's preoccupation with language and politics, while its title references the myth of two ancient Greek gods destined never to truly love each other, mirroring the tension between the band's punk roots and their pop aspirations .\n\nThe original album spawned five singles, including three UK Top 20 hits: \"Wood Beez (Pray Like Aretha Franklin),\" \"Absolute,\" and \"The Word Girl,\" alongside the US surprise hit \"Perfect Way,\" which reached number 11 on the Billboard Hot 100 . Hailed as a pinnacle of 1980s production, the record features lushly crafted tracks like \"Hypnotize\" and \"Absolute,\" showcasing nuanced layers of synth craftsmanship and soaring melodies that have been celebrated for their timelessness . In 2026, Rough Trade Records reissued the album as a Deluxe Edition, released on July 10, featuring a remastered version of the original album plus a series of extra tracks and remixes, bringing renewed attention to this classic of electronic and pop music .\n\nThis 2026 reissue by Rough Trade marks a significant moment for fans, offering a fresh auditory experience of Gartside's intoxicating melodies and the album's intricate production while preserving its historical importance as a high-water mark of 80s pop crossover . The reissue underscores the album's enduring legacy, which continues to sparkles after four decades, cementing Cupid & Psyche 85 as one of the most lushly produced and melodically uplifting records of its era . By combining the original's commercial success with",
